# {{SERVER_NAME}}

An HTTPS MCP server in Go, scaffolded with the safe-MCP playbook. Read tools and write tools are physically separated; mutations are off by default behind a single visible env switch; queries are bounded; AI search is rate-limited; all telemetry goes to stderr; errors are typed and actionable.

## Quickstart

    go mod tidy
    ./scripts/gen-dev-cert.sh        # one-time: localhost dev cert
    go run ./cmd/mcp-server          # HTTPS on port {{HTTPS_PORT}}
    ./scripts/inspector.sh           # stdio + MCP inspector UI
    go test ./...                    # unit + gate + normalization tests

## Environment variables

| Var                                     | Purpose                                                       | Default                  |
|-----------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------|
| `MCP_PORT`                              | HTTPS port                                                    | `{{HTTPS_PORT}}`         |
| `MCP_TLS_CERT` / `MCP_TLS_KEY`          | TLS material paths                                            | `./certs/dev-*.pem`      |
| `MCP_AUTH_MODE`                         | `oidc` / `api-key` / `both`                                   | `{{AUTH_MODE}}`          |
| `OIDC_ISSUER_URL` / `OIDC_AUDIENCE`     | OIDC validation                                               | unset (must set in prod) |
| `MCP_API_KEYS`                          | comma-separated keys, api-key mode only                       | unset                    |
| `BACKEND_BASE_URL`                      | upstream system of record                                     | `{{BACKEND_BASE_URL}}`   |
| `MCP_MUTATIONS_ENABLED`                 | **set to `true` to allow write tools**                        | `false`                  |
| `MCP_RATE_LIMIT_AI_SEARCH_PER_MIN`      | AI search per-user ceiling                                    | `6`                      |
| `MCP_MAX_RESULTS_CAP`                   | hard cap on search results                                    | `100`                    |

## Tool inventory

| Tool                  | Kind      | Notes                                                       |
|-----------------------|-----------|-------------------------------------------------------------|
| `search_companies`    | read      | Requires at least one filter; capped at 100 results.        |
| `get_company`         | read      | Returns `NOT_FOUND` typed error for unknown ids.            |
| `ai_search_companies` | read      | Rate-limited; configurable per-environment.                 |
| `create_ticket`       | write     | Off by default. Enable via `MCP_MUTATIONS_ENABLED=true`.    |

## The release-gate sequence

Before connecting any LLM client:

1. `go test ./...` — all tests green, including `TestMutationGate_GateClosed_BackendNotCalled`.
2. `./scripts/inspector.sh` — inspector opens, tool count matches the table.
3. Fire each read tool against the real backend. Confirm flat output shape.
4. With `MCP_MUTATIONS_ENABLED=false`: invoke `create_ticket`. Confirm `MUTATION_DISABLED` error mentions the env var.
5. With `MCP_MUTATIONS_ENABLED=true`: invoke `create_ticket` against a test backend. Confirm the success path.
6. Malformed input → `VALIDATION_FAILED` with a specific message.
7. AI search above the ceiling → `RATE_LIMITED` carrying the configured limit.

If any step fails, comment out the offending tool in `internal/tools/registry.go` with a `// FIXME(inspector):` note until fixed. Fail closed.

## Layout

    cmd/mcp-server/main.go        HTTPS + stdio entry, startup log line
    internal/
      config/                     env parsing into a typed Config
      auth/                       OIDC + api-key bearer verification
      logger/                     slog over stderr
      errors/                     typed error taxonomy
      ratelimit/                  per-user, per-tool token bucket
      pipeline/                   6-layer pipeline + AssertMutationsEnabled
      backends/
        client.go                 interface + typed records
        rest.go                   REST adapter
        graphql.go                GraphQL adapter
        grpc.go                   gRPC adapter stub
        fake.go                   recording fake for unit tests
      tools/
        registry.go               read tools first, mutations last
        search_companies.go       read
        get_company.go            read
        ai_search_companies.go    read (rate-limited)
        create_ticket.go          write (gated)
    tests/                        unit + gate + normalization tests

## Adding tools

Use the parent skill's `add-tool` mode. Hand-rolling new tools drifts the conventions.
